  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Evaluate $\\sqrt{3t+4}-\\sqrt[3]{9t+1}$ at $t=7.$",
  "worked_solution": "We replace $t$ with $7$ in the given expression, and simplify as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3t+4}-\\sqrt[3]{9t+1} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{3\\cdot 7+4}-\\sqrt[3]{9\\cdot 7+1} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{21+4}-\\sqrt[3]{63+1} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{25}-\\sqrt[3]{64} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{5}^{2}}-\\sqrt[3]{{4}^{3}} & = \\\\ 5-4 & = \\\\ 1 & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
